name issue_430_av_outage_6s
describe audio+video call, 6 s outage at 15 s on both paths: video returns at link-up or one 3 s decode timeout later, as libwebrtc (parity, #430)
# #430's 6 s variant. Two modes on both stacks: video back at link-up + 0.2 s, or one decode timeout later (+3.2 s)
# (#433's compare-webrtc, seeds 1-10, @ 0d86dcc): ours 4/10 seeds late, libwebrtc 3/10.
#   metric                ours mean (min-max)       libwebrtc mean (min-max)
#   video.pause_total_ms  7384 (6156-9240)          7076 (6156-9203)
#   video.render_fps      24.34 (22.88-25.28)       24.57 (22.98-25.25)
# Both stacks wait for the receiver's 3 s decode timeout (video_receive_stream2.cc kMaxWaitForFrame, OnDecodableFrameTimeout): the first keyframe request falls in the outage and is lost, the next one is sent 3 s later. The expect lines hold the call at libwebrtc's worst seed plus about 10 %.
# sm_compare runs 80 seeds here (#446): the 10-seed A/V offset p95 cell (98.4 vs 68.8 ms, band +-16.7, behind on 5/10)
# may be seed spread, as the #437 and #410 cells were; 80 seeds place it.
# Seeds 1-80 (#447, CI compare-webrtc at 42c1446), ours / libwebrtc: A/V offset p95 96.6 / 76.8 ms (libwebrtc sd 29.2),
# ours higher on 48/80: in band, so seed spread.
compare_seeds 80
seed 1
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
at 15s down
at 21s up
reverse at 0s delay=30ms
reverse at 15s down
reverse at 21s up
expect video.pause_total_ms < 10150
expect video.render_fps > 20.6
